linka/
# `case study/*`, not `case study/` — git never descends into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a negation below it can never match. Excluding the contents
# instead leaves the directory visible and the exception reachable.
case study/*
# ...except the Ledger, which is a TEST FIXTURE, not research.
# `tests/unit/ledgerCases.spec.ts` parses it and re-derives every verdict
# against `src/`, so an untracked copy means the suite passes here (Docker
# bind-mounts the working tree, ignored files included) and fails on a fresh
# clone with "no case rows parsed" — a green local run hiding a broken one.
!case study/LEDGER.md
node_modules/
dist/
screenshots/
playwright-report/
test-results/
# ANCHORED. Unanchored `demos/` also matched `tests/demos/`, which is SOURCE —
# the 199-demo runner, its arena factory and driver — so all five files sat
# silently untracked. The leading slash keeps the 53 MB of generated report
# output at the repo root excluded without reaching into `tests/`.
/demos/
.firebase/
.stl-scratch/
# Dead local state from the decommissioned Vercel setup — safe to delete by hand.
.vercel/
